<Window xmlns="clr-namespace:MGUI.Core.UI.XAML;assembly=MGUI.Core"
        Name="AlundraDialogue"
        Left="0" Top="0" Height="150"
        TitleText="Dialogue"
        IsCloseButtonVisible="False"
        IsTopmost="True"
        IsUserResizable="False"
        Padding="14"
        Background="rgba(12,18,26,235)">

  <!-- Alundra's dialogue box. It replaces the engine's built-in markup (CasaEngine's embedded
       DialogueScreen.xaml, from which it was copied): AlundraGame.json names this screen in its
       DialogueScreenAsset setting, written by the converter (parent ADR-0002, bound screens slice B4).

       The element names below are the engine dialogue screen's contract
       (CasaEngineMonogame/docs/engine/dialogue-choices-and-bitmap-fonts.md): pnlContent, lblLine and
       pnlChoices, with these types. One missing or declared with another type is not refused: the part it
       drives is simply not shown, and one warning names every such problem (decision D14). Only a markup
       that fails to load falls back to the built-in box.

       Left, Top and Height are starting values only. The screen centres the window horizontally, anchors it
       to the bottom, and sizes it to its content.

       No btnClose: Alundra's boxes are closed by the interact button or the auto timer, owned by
       AlundraDialogueDirector, never by a button in the box (AlundraDialoguePresenter sets
       ShowCloseButton to false). No title-bar close button either (IsCloseButtonVisible, D-E16-38,
       docs/plan-e16-etat-partie.md): the original has none, and closing the window from it left a choice
       asked without a box (the save screen's OUI/NON) waiting forever. -->

  <StackPanel Name="pnlContent" Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="8">

    <!-- No PreferredHeight on the panel: it must report its CONTENT height so the window's resize-to-fit
         measurement sees the real total. -->

    <TextBlock Name="lblLine" Text="" WrapText="True" FontSize="16" Foreground="White" />

    <StackPanel Name="pnlChoices" Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4" />

  </StackPanel>
</Window>
